An electron is travelling in a vacuum at a speed of $3.4 \times 10^7 \text{ m s}^{-1}$. The electron enters a region of uniform magnetic field of flux density $3.2 \text{ mT}$, as illustrated in Fig. 8.1.

{{figure:figure_8_1}}

The initial direction of the electron is at an angle of $30^{\circ}$ to the direction of the magnetic field.
